abstract: >-
  Code for generation, scoring and every analysis of the paper. The study
  measures the gain of chain-of-thought prompting against two direct-answer
  baselines: a requested answer, where the model is asked for the answer
  alone, and a forced answer, where the opening of the answer is written into
  the reply and the model may add only a few tokens. It runs open models on
  GSM8K, MATH-500, BIG-Bench Hard and HotpotQA under many prompt templates and
  counts how often the choice of baseline reverses which of two models gains
  more. The release includes a pilot tool that reports the share of long
  requested answers, the reliability of gains across templates, and who
  benefits under each baseline.
keywords:
